<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Irish Treaty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1921</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-war-of-independence">Irish War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Irish Treaty was signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> on 6 December 1921 by British ministers and Irish delegates led by Arthur Griffith and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-collins">Michael Collins</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-war-of-independence">Irish War of Independence</a>. It created the Irish Free State as a self-governing dominion, with an oath of fidelity to the crown, while Northern Ireland could opt out. Disagreement over it led to the Irish Civil War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-irish-treaty.jpg" alt="Anglo-Irish Treaty" width="320" height="505" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anglo-Irish_Treaty_signatures.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
